<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hergé</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1907–1983</span> · Also known as Georges Remi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hergé was the pen name of Georges Remi, a Belgian cartoonist best known for &quot;The Adventures of Tintin&quot;, which began in 1929. His clear-line drawing style shaped the Franco-Belgian comics tradition, and the series was translated into dozens of languages. His record during the German occupation, when Tintin appeared in a collaborationist newspaper, drew criticism after the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/herge.jpg" alt="Hergé" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonyme, revue italienne Linus, publiée en 1965. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Herge-Italie-1965-Linus.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
